=> Git Branching, Pull Request, Approval and Merge Workflow

    -> Purpose
        -> This workflow allows multiple developers to work safely on the same repository.
        -> Developers should not directly modify the main branch.
        -> Each developer creates a separate branch for their work.
        -> Changes are pushed to that branch.
        -> A Pull Request (PR) is created against main.
        -> The repository owner/reviewer reviews and approves the PR.
        -> After approval, the developer can merge the PR into main.
        -> After successful merge, the old working branch can be deleted.
        -> For the next task, a fresh branch should be created from the latest main.


