=> Step 13 – Create Pull Request

    -> Create PR from:

        akansha-updates
              |
              v
             main

    -> Using GitHub CLI:

        gh pr create --base main --head akansha-updates --title "SequencedCollection Update"

    -> Non-interactive command:

        gh pr create --base main --head akansha-updates --title "SequencedCollection Update" --body "Updated SequencedCollection notes and related file changes."

    -> Meaning:

        --base main
            -> Destination branch

        --head akansha-updates
            -> Source branch

        --title
            -> Pull Request title

        --body
            -> Pull Request description


=> Step 14 – Repository Main Branch Protection

    -> A GitHub Ruleset can protect main.

    -> Recommended rule:

        Require a pull request before merging

    -> Required approvals:

        1

    -> Recommended:

        Dismiss stale pull request approvals when new commits are pushed

    -> This means:

        Akansha creates PR
                |
                v
        Vinay approves
                |
                v
        Akansha pushes another commit
                |
                v
        Previous approval becomes invalid
                |
                v
        Vinay must review and approve again


=> Step 15 – Do NOT Enable Latest-Push Approval Requirement for This Workflow

    -> Option:

        Require approval of the most recent reviewable push

    -> Keep this disabled for the current workflow.

    -> Reason:

        If Vinay himself creates a branch and pushes the latest commit,
        GitHub could require another person to approve that latest push.

    -> Current requirement:

        Require Pull Request
        +
        Require 1 Approval


=> Step 16 – Repository Owner Reviews Pull Request

    -> Vinay opens the Pull Request.

    -> Review:

        Pull Request
            -> Files changed
            -> Review changes
            -> Approve
            -> Submit review

    -> After approval:

        Reviewers:
        Vinay8386 (Approved)


=> Step 17 – Verify Approval From Akansha Side

    -> From Akansha's CMD:

        gh pr view 1

    -> Example:

        Open
        Akansha8386 wants to merge into main
        Reviewers: Vinay8386 (Approved)

    -> This confirms the required approval has been completed.


=> Step 18 – Merge the Pull Request From Akansha Side

    -> After Vinay approves, Akansha can merge the PR.

    -> Run:

        gh pr merge 1

    -> GitHub CLI may provide merge methods:

        Merge commit
        Squash and merge
        Rebase and merge

    -> For normal collaborative workflow:

        Merge commit

    -> Important:

        Akansha creates the PR.
        Vinay reviews and approves it.
        Akansha performs the final merge.


=> Step 19 – What Happens After Merge

    -> Before merge:

        main
        |
        +--- existing code


        akansha-updates
        |
        +--- existing code
        +--- new Akansha changes


    -> After PR merge:

        main
        |
        +--- existing code
        +--- Akansha changes

    -> Therefore the latest approved code is now available in main.


=> Step 20 – Delete Old Working Branch

    -> After successful merge, the completed branch is no longer needed.

    -> Delete remote branch:

        git push origin --delete akansha-updates

    -> Delete local branch.

    -> First switch away from it:

        git checkout main

    -> Then delete:

        git branch -d akansha-updates

    -> -d performs safe deletion.

    -> Git normally prevents deletion if the branch contains unmerged work.


=> Step 21 – Update Local Main After Merge

    -> After the Pull Request is merged:

        git checkout main

    -> Download the latest merged main:

        git pull origin main

    -> Verify:

        git status

    -> Expected:

        On branch main
        Your branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.
        nothing to commit, working tree clean


=> Step 22 – Start Akansha's Next Task

    -> Never continue new work on an old completed branch.

    -> Start from latest main:

        git checkout main

        git pull origin main

    -> Create a fresh branch:

        git checkout -b akansha-new-task

    -> Then repeat:

        Make Changes
