=> Complete Recommended Workflow

    -> Start from latest main:

        git checkout main

        git pull origin main


    -> Create new branch:

        git checkout -b akansha-new-task


    -> Make changes.


    -> Check changes:

        git status


    -> Stage:

        git add .


    -> Commit:

        git commit -m "Updated required functionality"


    -> Push first time:

        git push -u origin akansha-new-task


    -> Create PR:

        gh pr create --base main --head akansha-new-task --title "Updated required functionality" --body "Updated required functionality."


    -> Vinay reviews and approves the Pull Request.


    -> Check PR:

        gh pr view <PR-NUMBER>


    -> After approval, Akansha merges:

        gh pr merge <PR-NUMBER>


    -> Switch to main:

        git checkout main


    -> Update local main:

        git pull origin main


    -> Delete local old branch:

        git branch -d akansha-new-task


    -> Delete remote old branch if it was not automatically deleted:

        git push origin --delete akansha-new-task


=> Important Rule

    -> Do NOT use this collaborative workflow:

        git checkout main
        git merge akansha-updates
        git push origin main

    -> Because this directly merges locally and pushes into main.

    -> Instead use:

        Feature Branch
              |
              v
        Pull Request
              |
              v
        Review
              |
              v
        Approval
              |
              v
        Merge PR

    -> This allows GitHub branch protection/rulesets to control changes to main.


=> Git Issues and Resolutions


    -> Issue 1 – Not a Git Repository

        -> Observation:

            fatal: not a git repository
            (or any of the parent directories): .git

        -> Cause:

            Command was executed outside the Git repository.

        -> Example:

            D:\Vinay_git_repo>

        -> Repository was actually:

            D:\Vinay_git_repo\core_Java

        -> Resolution:

            cd core_Java

            git status


    -> Issue 2 – Git Author Identity Unknown

        -> Observation:

            Author identity unknown

            Please tell me who you are.

        -> Cause:

            Git user.name and user.email were not configured.

        -> Resolution for shared computer:

            git config user.name "Akansha"

            git config user.email "Akansha-GitHub-Email"

        -> Do not use --global when different users may work from the same machine/repository environment.


    -> Issue 3 – GitHub Push Permission Denied

        -> Observation:

            Permission to Vinay8386/core_Java.git denied to Akansha8386.

            HTTP 403

        -> Cause:

            Akansha was authenticated correctly,
            but did not have write permission to Vinay's repository.

        -> Resolution:

            Vinay adds Akansha8386 as repository collaborator.

            Akansha accepts invitation.

            Then retry:

            git push -u origin akansha-updates


    -> Issue 4 – Branch Divergence

        -> Observation:

            Your branch and 'origin/main' have diverged.

        -> Cause:

            Local main and remote main contain different commits.

        -> Resolution:

            git checkout main

            git pull origin main

        -> Resolve conflicts if required.

        -> Then continue normally.


    -> Issue 5 – Push Rejected Because Local Branch Is Behind

        -> Observation:

            Updates were rejected because the tip of your current branch is behind.

        -> Cause:

            Remote contains newer commits that local branch does not contain.

        -> Resolution:

            git pull origin <branch-name>

        -> Resolve conflicts if required.

        -> Then:

            git push


    -> Issue 6 – Nothing Added to Commit

        -> Observation:

            nothing added to commit but untracked files present

        -> Cause:

            Files were changed or created but were not staged.

        -> Resolution:

            git status

            git add <file-name>

        -> Or:

            git add .

        -> Then:

            git commit -m "Commit message"


    -> Issue 7 – Wrong Branch Name During Merge

        -> Observation:

            merge: feature_branch - not something we can merge

        -> Cause:

            The specified branch does not exist.

        -> Resolution:

            git branch

        -> Verify the correct branch name before using it.


    -> Issue 8 – Linux Commands Not Working in Windows CMD

        -> Observation:

            'grep' is not recognized as an internal or external command.

        -> Cause:

            grep is normally a Linux/Unix command.

        -> Windows CMD alternatives:

            dir

            git branch

        -> PowerShell provides additional filtering capabilities when required.


    -> Issue 9 – GitHub CLI Not Found

        -> Observation:

            'gh' is not recognized as an internal or external command.

        -> Cause:

            GitHub CLI was not installed.

        -> Resolution:

            winget install --id GitHub.cli

        -> Open a new CMD after installation.

        -> Verify:

            gh --version


    -> Issue 10 – GitHub CLI Not Authenticated

        -> Resolution:

            gh auth login

        -> Login through browser.

        -> Verify:

            gh auth status


    -> Issue 11 – Merge Is Blocked

        -> Observation:

            Review required

            Merging is blocked

            At least 1 approving review is required

        -> This is NOT an error.

        -> It means the main branch ruleset is working correctly.

        -> Resolution:

            Vinay reviews the Pull Request.

            Vinay selects:

            Approve
            -> Submit review

        -> After approval, Akansha can merge the Pull Request.


